WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:15.512
Zann knew he should try to get away before the troll grabbed him.

2
00:00:16.232 --> 00:00:18.234
But the collision had knocked the breath out of him.

3
00:00:18.914 --> 00:00:22.877
All he could do was stare at the creature's broad chest, inches from his face.

4
00:00:23.617 --> 00:00:25.118
A glint of silver caught his eye.

5
00:00:25.818 --> 00:00:28.060
A small talisman hung around the troll's neck.

6
00:00:28.708 --> 00:00:33.352
It was slim and delicate, so tiny that Zann never would have spotted it from a distance.

7
00:00:34.493 --> 00:00:36.635
Zing let out a whistle and flew at the troll.

8
00:00:37.356 --> 00:00:41.319
Ignoring Zing's attack, the troll shoved Zann aside and hurried down the corridor.

9
00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:44.181
The troll hardly seemed to have noticed the kids at all.

10
00:00:44.942 --> 00:00:50.227
A puff of magic energy was floating above its ugly head, showing a chaotic image of running Reds

11
00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:51.608
and a pile of turnips.

12
00:00:51.628 --> 00:00:53.810
"Wow, that was close!"

13
00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:55.051
Gliss exclaimed.

14
00:00:55.071 --> 00:00:58.369
"Yeah. Why did that troll let me go?"

15
00:00:58.829 --> 00:00:59.410
Zann wondered.

16
00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:03.192
"It didn't even seem to see you," said Perda.

17
00:01:03.812 --> 00:01:05.413
Darb was staring after the creature.

18
00:01:05.433 --> 00:01:09.535
"Trolls have trouble thinking about more than one thing at a time," he said.

19
00:01:09.555 --> 00:01:14.077
"It looked like that one was running to tell Morb about the escaped prisoners at the zoo.

20
00:01:14.838 --> 00:01:16.959
It probably barely noticed we were in the way."

21
00:01:17.739 --> 00:01:19.560
"Lucky for us," Zann said.

22
00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.101
"Now let's get out of here!"

23
00:01:23.603 --> 00:01:26.064
Wyssa picked up the battered old brass pot.

24
00:01:26.836 --> 00:01:31.119
In Magica there was no need for the tonics and potions she'd learned to mix as a child.

25
00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:36.943
But she often needed such things in her travels, especially to those dangerous places that didn't have any

26
00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:37.864
natural magic.

27
00:01:38.604 --> 00:01:43.648
After placing the pot carefully into a large cloth bag, Wyssa straightened up with a groan.

28
00:01:44.348 --> 00:01:46.550
Years of traveling had been hard on her body.

29
00:01:47.651 --> 00:01:52.134
Her gaze fell on a worn blink image of a happy family, and she grimaced.

30
00:01:52.874 --> 00:01:55.016
Some of her travels had been hard on her soul too.

31
00:01:55.820 --> 00:02:01.622
Picking up the picture, she forced herself to stare at the smiling faces—especially that of the Red boy.

32
00:02:02.323 --> 00:02:04.764
Keeping the image around reminded her to be careful.

33
00:02:05.544 --> 00:02:08.625
That was why she was leaving the home she'd made for herself in Wormwood.

34
00:02:09.686 --> 00:02:11.687
And this time she wasn't coming back.

35
00:02:12.407 --> 00:02:17.169
She had one last errand to run, one last item she'd promised Morb.

36
00:02:17.909 --> 00:02:20.710
Then she was going somewhere he could never find her.

37
00:02:21.511 --> 00:02:24.852
Whatever happened next in Magica, she wouldn't be responsible.

38
00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:29.964
As she tucked the picture into her bag, Wyssa heard a shuffling step outside her hut.

39
00:02:30.584 --> 00:02:36.089
Looking out, she saw Hap staring curiously at the pile of objects she'd put outside the entrance.

40
00:02:36.109 --> 00:02:38.771
"Going somewhere, Wyssa?"

41
00:02:39.091 --> 00:02:41.373
the Void asked in his hoarse, high-pitched voice.

42
00:02:42.134 --> 00:02:45.697
"We're all going somewhere, my friend," she responded.

43
00:02:45.717 --> 00:02:51.462
"As for me, it's time for choice to put an end to what chance has started."

44
00:02:52.322 --> 00:02:53.203
Hap blinked at her.

45
00:02:54.744 --> 00:02:56.145
"Eh? What do you mean by that?"

46
00:02:56.925 --> 00:02:57.606
"Never mind."

47
00:02:58.366 --> 00:02:59.867
Wyssa waved an arm at the pile.

48
00:02:59.887 --> 00:03:03.729
"If there's anything you'd like in there, you're welcome to it.

49
00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:06.571
You can have my hut too, for that matter.

50
00:03:07.251 --> 00:03:11.153
You've been as good a neighbor as one could expect in a place like this."

51
00:03:12.054 --> 00:03:13.815
She cast a glance around Wormwood.

52
00:03:14.535 --> 00:03:15.456
She wouldn't miss it.

53
00:03:16.256 --> 00:03:17.537
Hap's eyes went wide.

54
00:03:17.557 --> 00:03:22.500
"My thanks to you, Wyssa," he said, shooting a greedy look at the hut.

55
00:03:23.252 --> 00:03:27.855
"It'll do my old bones good to have a roof over my head for a change."

56
00:03:28.996 --> 00:03:33.539
Wyssa went back inside just long enough to grab a few more items, which she stuffed into her

57
00:03:33.579 --> 00:03:35.501
bag. The rest didn't matter.

58
00:03:35.521 --> 00:03:41.525
"You're welcome," she told Hap, who was already admiring a frayed hat he'd found in the pile.

59
00:03:41.545 --> 00:03:44.527
"Good luck to you in the days ahead."

60
00:03:45.328 --> 00:03:50.151
Hap muttered another "thanks," though he didn't look up as Wyssa stepped toward the old tree without a

61
00:03:50.191 --> 00:03:50.932
backward glance.

62
00:03:53.844 --> 00:03:59.906
"I can't believe Morb just declared himself king like that," Perda said for about the tenth time since

63
00:04:00.126 --> 00:04:02.546
she, Zann, and the others had escaped from the palace.

64
00:04:02.566 --> 00:04:06.268
"It's not as if anybody could stop him," Gliss reminded her.

65
00:04:06.288 --> 00:04:08.348
"You saw what he did."

66
00:04:08.368 --> 00:04:10.609
"Yeah," Zann agreed.

67
00:04:10.629 --> 00:04:15.930
"He's got tons of power, all of it stolen from the Reds he kidnapped."

68
00:04:17.031 --> 00:04:21.932
Zann clenched his fists as he walked, thinking about Boz and Teplo and all the others.

69
00:04:22.908 --> 00:04:27.472
"Not to mention those horrible little dragons and all those trolls," Darb added.

70
00:04:28.273 --> 00:04:31.315
Zann shuddered when he thought back to his close call with the troll.

71
00:04:31.335 --> 00:04:34.678
"Hey, that reminds me," he said.

72
00:04:34.698 --> 00:04:38.761
"The troll I ran into was wearing a talisman around its neck.

73
00:04:39.582 --> 00:04:44.446
I've been wondering if that's how Morb is feeding the extra magical energy to the trolls.

74
00:04:45.546 --> 00:04:47.468
Maybe all of them are wearing talismans."

75
00:04:48.489 --> 00:04:52.232
"That would explain why the trolls have so much power," said Perda.

76
00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:58.285
"It might also explain how Morb is able to feed magic to them remotely," said Zann.

77
00:04:58.946 --> 00:05:02.970
"They became more powerful when we were at the zoo, and Morb wasn't even there."

78
00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:06.513
"We should tell Fala about this," said Darb.

79
00:05:06.533 --> 00:05:09.496
"She might know how talismans like that work."

80
00:05:10.557 --> 00:05:13.780
They'd slowed to a walk a couple of blocks earlier to catch their breath.

81
00:05:14.581 --> 00:05:17.864
The mention of Fala's name reminded Zann that they needed to hurry.

82
00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:22.881
The sooner they told Fala what was happening, the sooner she could help them think of a plan.

83
00:05:22.901 --> 00:05:26.022
"Come on, let's run," he suggested.

84
00:05:27.103 --> 00:05:30.704
Zing let out a whistle, flying faster as the kids broke into a jog.

85
00:05:31.724 --> 00:05:34.365
Soon they were just a few blocks from the safe house.

86
00:05:34.385 --> 00:05:37.786
"I hope Fala's back by now," Gliss said.

87
00:05:38.606 --> 00:05:39.587
Zann hoped so too.

88
00:05:40.347 --> 00:05:44.172
He also hoped that Fala would have some ideas for stopping Morb.

89
00:05:44.192 --> 00:05:49.906
Because with the palace under Morb's control and most Reds trapped in Morb's dungeon, Zann and his friends

90
00:05:49.986 --> 00:05:52.011
were probably Magica's only hope.
